\\\\ & =60\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18d61485-2e83-5936-bf4f-bdb56bc3c4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "972\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518910} {:answer/id #uuid "1c320d3a-60da-5b71-a776-74db91358bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{486}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518911} {:answer/id #uuid "45580a5e-5bf5-591a-975f-b5c6caffce26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "243\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518924} {:answer/id #uuid "981bec3c-d327-540d-b022-7683af7469d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "486\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518949} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f24ccd-920b-5556-ac5f-da611e02a4e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "236196\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "981bec3c-d327-540d-b022-7683af7469d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "486\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518949} :answer-field/id #uuid "f515b64d-d940-5cd5-9894-9abe522a7fe6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518973}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "829d2336-b2c1-5d22-81da-62efc70bcbb3" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-1,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\longrightarrow[\\begin{aligned}\\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{3}\\\\\\left(u - v\\right)^{2}\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =\\left|\\begin{matrix}3 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}&6 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}\\\\2 \\left(u - v\\right)&- 2 \\left(u - v\\right)\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =(3 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2})\\cdot (- 2 \\left(u - v\\right))-(6 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2})\\cdot (2 \\left(u - v\\right))\\\\& =- 18 u^{3} - 54 u^{2} v + 72 v^{3}\\\\& =- 18 \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-1,2)} & =\\left(- 18 \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}\\right)\\big|_{u=-1,v=2}\\\\& =- 18 \\left((-1) - (2)\\right) \\left((-1) + 2 (2)\\right)^{2}\\\\& =486\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|486|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =486\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518946 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09aa9167-b044-5501-8f63-4ce19c39ae5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518905} {:answer/id #uuid "09d9affe-0d42-57ca-8777-3fbb4b43fa8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518906} {:answer/id #uuid "979d8129-4d6e-5b64-adf3-cad4bb9f306b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32400\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518948} {:answer/id #uuid "c371dc56-8562-5f1d-88cd-cbe72dc4bff0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518961} {:answer/id #uuid "d50691b4-12ca-58c1-819c-2360e3254157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{180}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09aa9167-b044-5501-8f63-4ce19c39ae5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518905} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ac21d89-71cb-55af-8bb2-ae949d77431d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518942}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8a1a276c-9bc8-5768-90c3-2e3e48e45da7" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-2,1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\longrightarrow[\\begin{aligned}2 \\left(u + v\\right)^{3}\\\\\\left(2 u - v\\right)^{2}\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =\\left|\\begin{matrix}6 \\left(u + v\\right)^{2}&6 \\left(u + v\\right)^{2}\\\\4 \\left(2 u - v\\right)&- 2 \\left(2 u - v\\right)\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =(6 \\left(u + v\\right)^{2})\\cdot (- 2 \\left(2 u - v\\right))-(6 \\left(u + v\\right)^{2})\\cdot (4 \\left(2 u - v\\right))\\\\& =- 72 u^{3} - 108 u^{2} v + 36 v^{3}\\\\& =- 36 \\left(u + v\\right)^{2} \\left(2 u - v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-2,1)} & =\\left(- 36 \\left(u + v\\right)^{2} \\left(2 u - v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=-2,v=1}\\\\& =- 36 \\left((-2) + (1)\\right)^{2} \\left(2 (-2) - (1)\\right)\\\\& =180\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|180|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =180\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518954 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e43eb16-fd50-58a8-a646-55a7b162847a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518927} {:answer/id #uuid "5078973b-c6bc-557e-bd48-736bc3b4c202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{180}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518928} {:answer/id #uuid "5ea468ed-e1fe-5ba2-9fa5-fefe32cc95ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32400\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518934} {:answer/id #uuid "69db795c-5742-5b39-9574-c13288983347" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518938} {:answer/id #uuid "93bb489d-c9e5-5d96-b8d7-5033a9c1010a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69db795c-5742-5b39-9574-c13288983347" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518938} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0f839a4-8628-5b5f-ac1d-b0991c234235" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518971}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a969598c-ea80-5e43-ada9-6b7308b83589" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-2,-1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\longrightarrow[\\begin{aligned}2 \\left(2 u + v\\right)^{2}\\\\\\left(u - v\\right)^{3}\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =\\left|\\begin{matrix}8 \\left(2 u + v\\right)&4 \\left(2 u + v\\right)\\\\3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2}&- 3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =(8 \\left(2 u + v\\right))\\cdot (- 3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2})-(4 \\left(2 u + v\\right))\\cdot (3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2})\\\\& =- 72 u^{3} + 108 u^{2} v - 36 v^{3}\\\\& =- 36 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2} \\left(2 u + v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-2,-1)} & =\\left(- 36 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2} \\left(2 u + v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=-2,v=-1}\\\\& =- 36 \\left(- (-1) + (-2)\\right)^{2} \\left((-1) + 2 (-2)\\right)\\\\& =180\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|180|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =180\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518955 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15dbf132-3e31-59b6-b187-892685acc97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518909} {:answer/id #uuid "697e6aef-9964-5053-b382-5c88b21c2920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518937} {:answer/id #uuid "83524c04-5468-53fa-bd7d-bb4999cc9585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1936\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518945} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d2a6d9-d644-5d45-8bdf-1c1fb6df4980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518953} {:answer/id #uuid "f639046b-b2fc-5455-96d0-1286ffd8950a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{44}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "697e6aef-9964-5053-b382-5c88b21c2920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518937} :answer-field/id #uuid "535e0d1f-0eed-5a50-9f3c-40a846b5562f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518929}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "adc92b5f-6402-53d1-8666-3baacdfe2c66" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-2,-1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\longrightarrow[\\begin{aligned}2 u v^{3}\\\\u^{2} + v^{2}\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =\\left|\\begin{matrix}2 v^{3}&6 u v^{2}\\\\2 u&2 v\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =(2 v^{3})\\cdot (2 v)-(6 u v^{2})\\cdot (2 u)\\\\& =- 12 u^{2} v^{2} + 4 v^{4}\\\\& =- 4 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - v^{2}\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-2,-1)} & =\\left(- 4 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - v^{2}\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=-2,v=-1}\\\\& =- 4 (-1)^{2} \\left(- (-1)^{2} + 3 (-2)^{2}\\right)\\\\& =-44\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-44|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =44\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518958 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22ec1407-5d3e-572e-b894-a96fde5d8e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518912} {:answer/id #uuid "33d42482-34ef-59e1-9d7b-c0a1dcf6db23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518916} {:answer/id #uuid "39480101-3dbb-5f98-9d35-a02e91aadd76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518917} {:answer/id #uuid "3e0670ce-c1db-5e79-a6f4-2e53c985344b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{150}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518919} {:answer/id #uuid "3ffa3aa9-000d-52d4-8910-4d539df8e087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22500\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39480101-3dbb-5f98-9d35-a02e91aadd76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518917} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae334581-cc02-5854-80ac-65ba5fd211c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518956}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b11a00bf-ad16-5270-bbbf-f403e6fe76c2" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(3,1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\longrightarrow[\\begin{aligned}3 u v^{3}\\\\u^{2} + 2 v^{2}\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =\\left|\\begin{matrix}3 v^{3}&9 u v^{2}\\\\2 u&4 v\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =(3 v^{3})\\cdot (4 v)-(9 u v^{2})\\cdot (2 u)\\\\& =- 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 12 v^{4}\\\\& =- 6 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(3,1)} & =\\left(- 6 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=3,v=1}\\\\& =- 6 (1)^{2} \\left(- 2 (1)^{2} + 3 (3)^{2}\\right)\\\\& =-150\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-150|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =150\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a46dd2e-7844-511c-8225-1d0a51bb3eaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518918} {:answer/id #uuid "421250cd-a2d2-59cf-a6de-47aaded334b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20736\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518922} {:answer/id #uuid "549b51aa-02b7-56c9-a3ea-cc9c797d0dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{144}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518931} {:answer/id #uuid "5c59fc35-b29f-5893-8340-a07c39c6bbb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518933} {:answer/id #uuid "ec16d3f2-9da5-5e85-813f-086fbb3e74c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "288\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c59fc35-b29f-5893-8340-a07c39c6bbb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518933} :answer-field/id #uuid "e48954b8-5146-577a-919f-6d9a5e7fbd72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518967}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dcaa4bdd-7f4f-5106-9de8-2ca23f1745cd" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1,-1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\longrightarrow[\\begin{aligned}2 \\left(2 u + v\\right)^{2}\\\\\\left(u - v\\right)^{3}\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =\\left|\\begin{matrix}8 \\left(2 u + v\\right)&4 \\left(2 u + v\\right)\\\\3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2}&- 3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\& =(8 \\left(2 u + v\\right))\\cdot (- 3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2})-(4 \\left(2 u + v\\right))\\cdot (3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2})\\\\& =- 72 u^{3} + 108 u^{2} v - 36 v^{3}\\\\& =- 36 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2} \\left(2 u + v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(1,-1)} & =\\left(- 36 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2} \\left(2 u + v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=1,v=-1}\\\\& =- 36 \\left(- (-1) + (1)\\right)^{2} \\left((-1) + 2 (1)\\right)\\\\& =-144\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-144|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =144\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Local Area Scale Factor of a Transformation"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175693 :question/id #uuid "70569afd-42c4-5e5f-8397-4fbd873eb8e4" :question/math-academy-id "e-11002" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The range of the function is $[-1,1].$\n\n- The function has minimum values at $x =n\\pi.$\n\n- The function intersects the $x$-axis at $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} +\\pi n.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos{x}.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$ Therefore, the range is $[-1,1].$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has a minimum at $x=\\pi$ and the period is $2\\pi.$ Therefore, the minimum values occur at $\\pi+2n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement III is true. These are the zeros of the cosine curve. The cosine curve has zeros at $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi.$\n\nIn conclusion, only statements I and III are true."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050033 :topic/math-academy-id 2707 :topic/title "Local Extrema of Functions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050718 :topic/math-academy-id 1491 :topic/title "Graphing Sine and Cosine"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3b87e3a-d17f-5d16-a9ee-8bdda6d42f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439603} {:answer/id #uuid "87018b61-01ec-510f-8fd1-7d6db056af27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3b87e3a-d17f-5d16-a9ee-8bdda6d42f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439603} :answer-field/id #uuid "d542c682-d8b5-5051-a7cb-60f1509b7b1e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d64fb74-88cb-53a7-a06c-3b70bb7f6274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439605} {:answer/id #uuid "bec31bb0-4e5d-511d-afd5-742b83de0357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/t