 the function has value $\\cos 0=1$.\n\n- Statement II is true. $\\cos(\\frac{\\pi}{2})=0$.\n\n- Statement III is false. $\\cos(\\pi)=-1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512069 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42868a5d-2294-5aba-8bc3-3903089d47fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512009} {:answer/id #uuid "c8669141-affc-5f16-aba9-f7dd4716a792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8669141-affc-5f16-aba9-f7dd4716a792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512064} :answer-field/id #uuid "32048f4b-d6e3-557a-b273-69b36821429d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512000} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67e05fc1-6f27-5a55-b0b8-2454bb824ea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512022} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d3bbf8-afc9-50d1-a551-cec7b4370f7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67e05fc1-6f27-5a55-b0b8-2454bb824ea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512022} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a1d64d3-cc73-5c25-8f75-374c7c718c4a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3aa5caf5-667a-5d0e-b3dd-09947d8deafd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512002} {:answer/id #uuid "4464d916-5dd5-58e9-a4d3-34f78b7e2336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4464d916-5dd5-58e9-a4d3-34f78b7e2336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512011} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f7f8471-d306-5267-a916-084d0ff2554f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512051}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e62133c8-9957-522b-ac43-c73e3353a608" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\pi.$\n- **II.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=n\\pi.$\n- **III.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has minimum values is $x=\\pi+2n\\pi.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi$. Every zero must be included.\n\n- Statement II is false. The maximum value is $1$, attained at $x=2n\\pi$. Every maximum input must be included.\n\n- Statement III is true. The minimum value is $-1$, attained at $x=\\pi+2n\\pi$. Every minimum input must be included."}] :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176048 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175694 :question/id #uuid "a8cc8b8f-463b-5734-a33d-e915159cba32" :question/math-academy-id "e-11003" :question/problem "If $\\cos x =- \\dfrac {1}{3},$ find the value of $2\\cos( x + 4\\pi)+3.$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y = \\cos x$ is $2\\pi.$ Therefore, for any integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos{x} = \\cos{(x+2n\\pi)} .\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=2$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡x & =cos⁡(x+2\\cdot 2\\cdot \\pi ) \\\\  & =cos⁡(x+4\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cos{x} =- \\dfrac {1}{3},$ then $\\cos{(x+4\\pi)} = - \\dfrac {1}{3}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2cos⁡(x+4\\pi )+3 & =2(-\\frac{1}{3})+3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}+3 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c25c3a0-083a-55d5-b688-7347bfafaa9e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049353 :topic/math-academy-id 2148 :topic/title "Periodic Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88f28e6a-97ea-5e36-bf74-369bcac3c4bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175415} {:answer/id #uuid "9e88cd39-4060-5bbd-a35c-9862da2c6a1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175416} {:answer/id #uuid "9fd05264-d89f-5106-8257-5d4ac26b1665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175417} {:answer/id #uuid "20110d5e-fbba-58e2-8b26-14f37290f7e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175418} {:answer/id #uuid "778b3ce5-f938-535a-88ae-9093fb35824b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175419}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d12dd988-13f0-5a13-904a-161740f16df7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175414}] :question/id #uuid "5457cf58-f029-55a0-8895-b6f3142a17ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-65176" :question/problem "If $\\cos x = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$, then $4\\cos (x - 6π) - 1 =$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176547 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c52f2c48-4a46-5583-880d-822ccf44143f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175421} 